.\" Manual page for pcloudd(1) - the pCloud background daemon.
.\" Lint with: groff -ww -man -Tutf8 packaging/man/pcloudd.1 >/dev/null
.TH PCLOUDD 1 "April 16, 2026" "pcloud-rs-rust" "pCloud Client Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.
.SH NAME
pcloudd \- pCloud background service daemon (Rust rewrite)
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcloudd
.br
.B pcloudd
.B serve
.br
.B pcloudd
.RB { \-\-help | \-h | help }
.br
.B pcloudd
.RB { \-\-version | \-V | version }
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcloudd
is the long-running background service that owns every piece of state a
pCloud client needs: the local IPC socket, the auth-token vault, the
SQLite state store, the transfer/sync/crypto/shares runtimes, the
observability exporters, and \(em once the FUSE parity work (tracker
bead
.BR bd\-1du.4 )
lands \(em the mounted-drive runtime. Interactive control flows
exclusively through
.BR pcloudc (1)
over a Unix-domain socket: operators only run
.B pcloudd
themselves to produce a one-shot bootstrap summary, or have a service
manager (systemd, launchd, SCM, rc.d) launch
.B pcloudd serve
on their behalf.
.
.SS Why a separate daemon at all
The pcloud-rs SDK is a library, but many of the guarantees the product
relies on can only be made by a long-lived process: (1) there must be a
single owner of the upload journal, crash-safe staging, and the SQLite
write lock; (2) the auth vault must live under a fixed UID so the
on-disk mode
.B 0600
check is meaningful; (3) TLS connections to the API, bandwidth pacing,
and retry schedules amortize only when amortized across requests; (4)
the FUSE mount, once wired, is a kernel-attached resource that cannot
migrate across processes. Splitting
.B pcloudd
from
.BR pcloudc (1)
also keeps the CLI free of ambient authority: the CLI is a thin
tool that can run as any user and is gated at the socket.
.
.SS Request lifecycle
.nf
  pcloudc (or SDK embedder)
        |
        |  JSON-encoded, length-prefixed frame on an owner-only AF_UNIX
        |  socket ($PCLOUD_ROOT/runtime/pcloudd.sock, mode 0600)
        v
  pcloud-ipc::IpcServer::accept
        |  peer-credential check (SO_PEERCRED on Linux,
        |  getpeereid(3) on *BSD/macOS, named-pipe SID DACL on Windows).
        |  Reject cross-UID peers.
        v
  pcloud-ipc::transport::read_frame
        |  Enforces 1 MiB (1_048_576 B) per-request cap
        |  (pcloud_ipc::MAX_REQUEST_BYTES) before allocating.
        v
  pcloud-daemon::dispatch::dispatch
        |  Optional W3C traceparent extraction (tracing-otlp feature);
        |  opens a pcloudd.dispatch span parented to caller.
        |  Routes Request -> backend runtime (auth/transfer/sync/crypto/
        |  public_link/shares/backup/account/notifications).
        v
  Backend runtime -> pcloud-proto HTTPS -> pCloud API (or local only).
        |
        v
  Response frame written back. Serve loop observes
  signals::shutdown_requested() between accepts and drains cleanly.
.fi
.
.SS Security model (one-line version)
Owner-only IPC socket, peer-UID gated on accept, 1 MiB request cap,
TLS-only in production, opt-in durable auth tokens in a
.B 0700
vault dir with per-file
.B 0600
mode, no cleartext password persistence, secret-bearing fields wrapped
in
.B SecretString
/
.B SecretBytes
(zeroize-on-drop, redacted
.BR Debug ).
.
.SS Persistence model
One SQLite file
.RI ( state/store.sqlite3 ),
one vault directory
.RI ( state/vault ),
one append-only audit log
.RI ( state/audit.log ),
and transient state under
.I runtime/
and
.IR cache/ .
The daemon runs
.B PRAGMA integrity_check
at bootstrap and surfaces the result on the first
.B Health
request.
.
.SH COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS
.B pcloudd
accepts a deliberately minimal argument surface. All runtime tuning
happens through
.BR pcloud.conf (5)
and
.B PCLOUD_*
environment variables, so the binary remains safe to ship with no
flags to audit.
.TP
.B (no argument)
.B Mode: Summary.
Bootstraps the runtime, prints the resolved configuration plus every
subsystem's health verdict, and exits 0. Does NOT bind the IPC socket.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Why:
verify on a fresh host that config discovery, directory modes, vault
permissions, store migrations, and credential bootstrap all succeed
before you ask systemd to flip the service on.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Failure modes:
any bootstrap error surfaces here exactly as it would in
.B serve
mode, but you get to fix it before a service manager starts
retry-looping.
.RE
.TP
.B serve
.B Mode: Serve.
Long-running. Installs SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP/SIGPIPE handlers
.B before
bootstrapping, bootstraps the runtime, binds the owner-only IPC
socket, optionally spawns the Prometheus scrape listener (feature
.BR metrics ),
and enters the dispatch loop. This is the mode every service manager
must launch.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h ", " help
Print the built-in help text and exit 0. Authoritative inventory of
the daemon's argument surface (mirrors this manpage's
.B SYNOPSIS ).
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V ", " version
Print
.RB \(dq pcloudd
.IR <cargo-pkg-version> \(dq
and exit 0. Use in packaging scripts and for release-note regressions.
.PP
Unknown arguments are rejected with exit
.BR 1 .
There are no hidden flags and no environment-only feature toggles that
are not also documented under
.B ENVIRONMENT
below.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The authoritative reference is
.BR pcloud.conf (5);
this section is an operator-level table of contents.
.B pcloudd
starts from
.BR ConfigProfile::secure_defaults ,
layers the on-disk
.I pcloud.toml
over it, applies any
.B PCLOUD_*
environment overrides via
.BR apply_env_overrides ,
then validates the result. Validation is strict: a production
environment that would end up on plaintext HTTP is rejected at
startup.
.TP
.B [profile]
Top-level envelope:
.B environment
(one of
.BR Production ,
.BR Development ,
.BR Test ).
Everything security-sensitive \(em TLS policy, metrics wildcard bind,
integrity sweeper cadence \(em keys off this. Operators should treat
.B Production
as the default and only flip to
.B Development
on dev boxes.
.TP
.B [profile.paths]
File-system layout:
.BR config_dir ,
.BR state_dir ,
.BR runtime_dir ,
.BR cache_dir .
Governed by
.BR PCLOUD_ROOT ;
see
.B FILES
below for modes and owners. Touch these only for containerized /
multi-tenant / test layouts.
.TP
.B [profile.api]
Upstream transport:
.BR mode ,
.BR host ,
.BR port ,
.BR server_name
(TLS SNI / cert verify),
.BR connect_timeout_ms ,
.BR read_timeout_ms .
Production mode refuses plaintext; overrides via
.B PCLOUD_API_*
are honored but re-validated.
.TP
.B [profile.features]
Product feature gates.
.B durable_auth_tokens_enabled
(the only field the daemon reads for security posture) defaults off.
.TP
.B [profile.features.integrity_sweeper]
Background worker that re-verifies on-disk state.
.BR enabled ,
.BR interval_seconds ,
.BR chunk_size .
Leave disabled unless you are debugging store corruption.
.TP
.B [profile.crypto]
Client-side-crypto subsystem parameters: KDF cost, AES-GCM sector
size. Sensible defaults; do not touch without a threat model.
.TP
.B [profile.crypto.kms]
KMS / HSM adapter selector. A
.B Pkcs11Hsm
variant is declared but is a stub in pre-alpha \(em the production path
is the built-in software-backed key wrapper.
.TP
.B [profile.data_residency]
Region pin for where user data should land. Enforced via API-server
selection and by refusing requests that would cross residency.
.TP
.B [profile.resilience]
Retry policy for the TLS transport: base backoff, jitter, maximum
attempts. Consumed by
.B TransportFactory
in production; development/test bypass the wrapper for test
determinism.
.TP
.B [profile.observability]
Metrics, tracing, and SLO knobs. See
.B OBSERVABILITY
below.
.TP
.B [profile.extensions]
Plugin registry gates. All four plugin booleans default off. Flip them
at your own risk \(em capabilities granted here are ambient to plugin
code.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every variable listed below is actually read by
.B pcloudd
or a crate it depends on (verified by grepping
.B std::env::var*
across
.I crates/pcloud-daemon
and
.IR crates/pcloud-config ).
Values are parsed at bootstrap; the daemon does not re-read the
environment after startup. A variable not listed here has no effect on
.BR pcloudd .
.TP
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
.RS
.IP "Purpose:" 14
Single-tree override for every managed directory. Sets
.BR config_dir ,
.BR state_dir ,
.BR runtime_dir ,
.BR cache_dir ,
and (when plugins are enabled)
.B plugin_dir
to
.IR <root>/{config,state,runtime,cache,plugins} .
.IP "Why:" 14
Multi-instance isolation, containers, test harnesses.
.IP "Default:" 14
unset (XDG/Library/AppData defaults apply).
.IP "Example:" 14
.B PCLOUD_ROOT=/var/lib/pcloud/alice
.IP "Failure:" 14
Parent not writable -> bootstrap directory provisioning fails.
.RE
.TP
.B PCLOUD_ENV
.RS
.IP "Purpose:" 14
Select environment semantics. Accepts
.IR dev / development ,
.IR test ,
.IR prod / production
(case-insensitive).
.IP "Why:" 14
Flips secure defaults (TLS on/off, metrics wildcard bind allowed,
etc.). Also snaps
.B api.mode
to the environment default
.B unless
.B PCLOUD_API_MODE
is also set.
.IP "Default:" 14
.B production
.IP "Failure:" 14
Unknown token -> config validation error, daemon aborts.
.RE
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_MODE
.RS
.IP "Purpose:" 14
Transport mode override. Values:
.BR tls ,
.BR plaintext ,
.BR development .
.IP "Why:" 14
Dev/CI can pin
.B plaintext
against a local stub; production
.B always
rejects anything that isn't TLS.
.IP "Failure:" 14
Plaintext in production -> bootstrap refuses to start.
.RE
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_HOST
Override
.B api.host
(e.g.
.BR binapi.pcloud.com ,
.BR eapi.pcloud.com ).
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_PORT
Override
.B api.port
(u16, 0 rejected).
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_SERVER_NAME
Override TLS SNI / certificate verification name. Only touch when
pinning a non-standard gateway.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
u64 milliseconds,
.B 0
rejected. Bounds initial TCP+TLS handshake.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_API_READ_TIMEOUT_MS
u64 milliseconds,
.B 0
rejected. Bounds per-read on the established TLS stream.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS
Boolean (
.IR 1 / 0 ,
.IR true / false ,
.IR yes / no ,
.IR on / off ).
Opt-in to on-disk auth-token persistence under the vault. Off by
default. When off, a restart requires re-auth. Plaintext passwords are
.B never
persisted regardless of this flag.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_VAULT
Backend selector for the token vault. Values:
.BR file
(default),
.B secret-service
(XDG DBus keyring, where available). The
.B secret-service
backend falls back to file with an audit line if DBus is unavailable.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_CACHE_SIZE_GB
Runtime ceiling (in GiB) for the upload/download cache. Parsed at
runtime init. Non-numeric values are ignored with a log line.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY
Key material (treated as opaque bytes) for HMAC-signing every audit
record. When present the audit log is a hash
.B and
HMAC chain; when absent it is a hash chain only. The audit verifier
(\c
.B pcloudc audit verify\c
) requires the same key to validate HMACs.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_FORCE_UMOUNT
Boolean. If set, an orphaned FUSE mount left behind by a SIGKILLed or
crashed daemon is force-unmounted during startup instead of blocking
the mount service. Prefer the
.B pcloudc mount --force-umount <path>
command for targeted recovery.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_METRICS_PORT
(feature
.BR metrics )
Loopback port for the Prometheus scrape listener. Default
.BR 9353 .
Setting
.B 0
picks an ephemeral port (used by tests).
.TP
.B PCLOUD_METRICS_BIND_ALL
(feature
.BR metrics )
Bind the metrics exporter on
.B 0.0.0.0
instead of
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.B Refused
when
.B PCLOUD_ENV
is not
.B development
\(em production scrapers must reach the daemon via loopback, a local
reverse proxy, or a mesh sidecar.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_PLUGINS_ENABLED
Boolean. Gate for the entire plugin registry. Off by default.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_NETWORK
Boolean. Grants plugins the network capability. Requires
.BR plugins_enabled=true .
.TP
.B PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_SYNC_CONTROL
Boolean. Grants plugins sync-control authority.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_CRYPTO
Boolean. Grants plugins direct crypto authority. Strongly discouraged.
.TP
.B PCLOUD_MIGRATE_LEGACY_PATHS
Boolean. One-shot migration from the legacy C-client on-disk layout
into the new XDG tree. Safe to run repeatedly; a no-op if nothing is
left to migrate.
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_TOKEN_FILE
Path to a file containing a bearer auth token used for headless
bootstrap. File must be a regular file, owned by the effective UID,
mode
.B 0600
(no group/other bits). Content is UTF-8, trimmed of whitespace, and
wrapped in
.B SecretString
before use. Buffer is zeroized on error.
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_USERNAME_FILE
Path to a file containing the pCloud account email. Same permission
rules as
.BR PCLOUDRS_TOKEN_FILE .
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_PASSWORD_FILE
Path to a file containing the account password. Same permission rules.
The password is consumed into a
.B SecretString
at bootstrap and zeroized after the login round-trip; it is
.B never
written to disk.
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_TFA_CODE_FILE
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_RECOVERY_CODE_FILE
Mutually exclusive. File-backed second-factor secret for non-interactive
TFA flows. Setting both is an error.
.TP
.B PCLOUDRS_TRUST_DEVICE
Boolean. Tells the TFA flow to remember this device after a successful
second-factor, so subsequent daemons on the same install do not
re-prompt.
.TP
.B CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
systemd-managed directory containing unit
.B LoadCredential=
files. When set, the daemon will look for
.IR pcloud-rs-token ,
.IR pcloud-rs-username ,
.IR pcloud-rs-password ,
.IR pcloud-rs-tfa-code ,
and
.I pcloud-rs-recovery-code
inside it as fallbacks for the
.B PCLOUDRS_*_FILE
variables.
.TP
.B HOME
Consumed by
.B PcloudDirs::discover()
on Linux/BSD to form the XDG defaults; ignored when
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
is set.
.PP
Variables prefixed
.B PCLOUD_OBSERVABILITY_
are reserved for the observability layer and map directly to
.B [profile.observability]
keys; see
.BR pcloud.conf (5).
.
.SH SIGNALS
Installed by
.B pcloud_daemon::signals::install_default_handlers
.B before
subsystem bootstrap so even a slow bootstrap can be interrupted
cleanly without tripping
.BR "systemd TimeoutStopSec" .
Handlers are async-signal-safe: they flip atomic flags, nothing more.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown request. Sets
.BR SHUTDOWN_REQUESTED ;
the serve loop observes the flag between
.BR accept (2)
calls (blocking
.B accept
returns
.B EINTR
because
.B SA_RESTART
is intentionally not set on these handlers), drains any in-flight IPC
request through the existing dispatch path, flushes the upload journal
and audit log, closes the store, unmounts where applicable, and exits
.BR 0 .
This is the signal service managers should send.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Same semantics as
.B SIGTERM .
Convenient for foreground / debug runs.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Triggers a hot-reload of the on-disk config file. The serve loop
re-reads the file, computes a diff of hot-reloadable fields, and
applies changes to: log level / observability flags, rate-limit
budgets, integrity-sweeper schedule, sync poll interval, and
data-residency allow-list. Fields that require a restart (auth vault
path, IPC socket path, crypto master key) are silently ignored.
On parse error the previous config is kept and a
.B config.reload_failed
audit event is emitted. On success a
.B config.reloaded
audit event lists the changed keys. Send via
.BR "pcloudc reload" .
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Explicitly ignored (\c
.BR SIG_IGN ).
Broken client sockets surface as
.B EPIPE
returns on the write-side inside dispatch.
.TP
.B SIGKILL
Do not send. Bypasses the shutdown path entirely; leaves the FUSE
mountpoint, upload journal sidecars, and vault file locks in recovery
state. See
.B TROUBLESHOOTING
and
.BR PCLOUD_FORCE_UMOUNT .
.PP
Signal-handler installation is idempotent and guarded by a
.BR std::sync::Once ;
a failure at install-time returns from
.B main
before any I/O happens and the daemon exits
.BR 1 .
.
.SH FILES
The table below lists every path the daemon touches. Ownership is the
effective UID of the
.B pcloudd
process; all directories and files are created by bootstrap if
missing.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/config/pcloud.toml
Primary configuration. Mode
.BR 0600 ,
parent dir mode
.BR 0700 .
See
.BR pcloud.conf (5).
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/runtime/pcloudd.sock
Owner-only Unix-domain IPC socket. Mode
.BR 0600 .
Binding fails if a stale socket exists that the current UID does not
own.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/runtime/
Runtime directory. Mode
.BR 0700 .
Holds the socket and any transient per-session state.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/state/
State directory. Mode
.BR 0700 .
Parent of everything durable.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/state/store.sqlite3
Primary persistent store: sync roots, device record, primary account,
preferences, audit chain head, upload resume index, integrity sweeper
cursor. Created on first launch, migrated in-place, integrity-checked
at bootstrap.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/state/vault/
Auth-token vault directory. Mode
.BR 0700 ;
per-file
.BR 0600 .
Populated only when
.B PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS=1
and a live session exists. Passwords are
.B never
stored here.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/state/audit.log
Append-only audit log. Each record carries the previous record's
hash; with
.B PCLOUD_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY
set, also an HMAC. Verified out-of-band by
.BR "pcloudc audit verify" .
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/cache/
Cache directory. Mode
.BR 0700 .
Bounded by
.BR PCLOUD_CACHE_SIZE_GB .
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/cache/fuse-staging/
FUSE write-path staging tree. Per-inode chunked-upload sidecars live
here. Scanned at bootstrap (\c
.BR enumerate_upload_sidecars );
live reconcile is driven once the mount comes up.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/cache/page-cache/
Read-side page cache (once FUSE lands under
.BR bd\-1du.4 ).
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/state/integrity_sweeper.cursor
Persistent cursor for the integrity sweeper service. Present only
when the sweeper is enabled.
.TP
.I $PCLOUD_ROOT/config/plugins/
Plugin drop-in directory. Created and set
.B 0700
only when
.BR PCLOUD_PLUGINS_ENABLED=1 .
.PP
Default
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
resolution:
.IR ~/.config/pcloud ,
.IR ~/.local/state/pcloud ,
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pcloud ,
.I ~/.cache/pcloud
on Linux/BSD;
.I ~/Library/...
on macOS;
.I %APPDATA%/%LOCALAPPDATA%
on Windows.
.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
.SS IPC socket
AF_UNIX, mode
.BR 0600 ,
owner = daemon UID. Binding uses
.B pcloud_ipc::IpcServer::new(current_effective_uid())
so the expected peer UID is captured at server construction. Every
accepted connection is then validated against that UID using the
platform-appropriate peer-credential primitive:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Linux:
.B getsockopt(SO_PEERCRED)
\(em returns kernel-enforced (pid, uid, gid) of the peer.
.IP \(bu 2
.B FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD, macOS:
.BR getpeereid (3)
\(em returns (euid, egid) of the peer.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Windows:
named-pipe plus SID DACL check. The pipe is opened with an explicit
DACL granting access to the owner SID only; the server additionally
asserts the authenticated client SID equals the owner SID before
accepting traffic.
.RE
Peers whose UID (or SID) does not match are rejected at accept-time
with
.BR ResponseStatus::Unauthorized ;
no request bytes are read.
.SS Request size cap
.B pcloud_ipc::MAX_REQUEST_BYTES
= 1 MiB = 1_048_576 B. Frames declaring more are rejected
.B before
buffer allocation, which bounds both memory and decode time. The
typed dispatcher then decodes JSON; malformed frames are rejected with
a typed error, never by panic.
.SS Secret handling
Secret-bearing fields \(em passwords, auth tokens, TFA codes, recovery
codes, crypto passphrase, HMAC key material as it passes through
memory \(em use
.B pcloud_secret::SecretString
and
.BR pcloud_secret::SecretBytes ,
both of which:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
redact to
.BR "REDACTED"
in
.BR Debug
output,
.IP \(bu 2
zeroize their buffers on
.BR Drop ,
.IP \(bu 2
require explicit
.B expose_secret()
to obtain the inner view.
.RE
Bootstrap also zeroizes the raw file buffer before returning when a
.B PCLOUDRS_*_FILE
is read.
.SS Auth-token vault
Durable persistence is
.B off
by default. When enabled (\c
.BR PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS=1 ),
the vault directory is
.B 0700
and each token file is
.BR 0600 ;
both are re-checked on load. A vault with the wrong mode or owner is
rejected. Passwords are
.B never
persisted.
.SS Transport policy
Production mode rejects any config, on-disk or env-driven, that would
yield a non-TLS transport. The
.B ResilientTransport
wrapper (retry + jitter) is applied in production only; development
and test keep the bare transport for test determinism.
.SS Metrics listener
Defaults to loopback
.RB ( 127.0.0.1 ).
Wildcard bind requires
.B BOTH
.BR PCLOUD_METRICS_BIND_ALL=1
.B AND
.B Environment::Development
\(em production config cannot be coerced into exposing
.I /metrics
off-host.
.SS Audit log
Every security-relevant action the daemon takes appends one record to
.IR state/audit.log .
Each record carries the SHA-256 of the previous record (hash chain).
When
.B PCLOUD_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY
is set, records are additionally HMAC-signed with that key; the key
must be re-supplied to the verifier. A mid-chain tamper is detected on
.B pcloudc audit verify.
.
.SH OBSERVABILITY
.SS Metrics (feature
.BR metrics )
.B pcloudd serve
spawns a Prometheus scrape listener in parallel with the IPC loop.
Default bind is
.BR 127.0.0.1:9353 .
Endpoints:
.TP
.I /metrics
Prometheus text format. Families include request counters by method,
per-backend latency histograms (notably
.BR flush_latency_seconds ),
transport retry counters, and the integrity sweeper progress gauge.
.TP
.I /slo
Operator-friendly JSON summary of the in-memory SLO registry. Empty
until the runtime begins handling requests.
.TP
.I /health
Liveness bit. Returns 200 while the serve loop is clean; non-200
after shutdown begins.
.SS Tracing (feature
.BR tracing-otlp )
W3C Trace Context propagated from
.BR pcloudc (1)
is extracted by
.B RequestEnvelope::try_from_wire
and installed on the dispatch thread via
.BR set_thread_traceparent .
Each dispatched request opens:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
a
.B pcloudd.dispatch
server span parented to the inbound traceparent (or a fresh root if
none / unparseable),
.IP \(bu 2
an internal
.BI pcloudd.backend. name
span per handler, where
.I <name>
is drawn from a stable allow-list (\c
.IR auth ,
.IR crypto ,
.IR sync ,
.IR transfer ,
.IR public_link ,
.IR shares ,
.IR backup ,
.IR account ,
.IR control ,
.IR notifications ,
.IR other ).
.IP \(bu 2
a
.BI pcloud.proto. method
client span per upstream HTTPS call.
.RE
All span attributes flow through
.B pcloud_observability::tracing::attr_redact
which enforces an allow-list (\c
.BR command ,
.BR duration_ms ,
.BR error_category ,
.BR status_code ,
.BR trace_kind ).
Any other key is dropped in release builds and panics in debug builds
so violations are caught in CI; there is no code path that emits a
filename, path, email, auth token, or key material through an
attribute.
.PP
Configure under
.B [profile.observability.tracing]
in
.BR pcloud.conf (5):
.B endpoint
must be
.B https://
unless loopback;
.B sample_rate
is clamped to
.BR [0.0,1.0] ;
.B headers
values must use the
.B ${env:VAR}
form (literal values are refused at startup).
.SS Audit log
Hash-chained, optionally HMAC-signed. See
.B SECURITY MODEL
above. Verify with
.BR "pcloudc audit verify" .
.
.SH IPC PROTOCOL
Wire-level reference:
.I docs/book/src/reference/ipc-protocol.md
(repository tree). Summary:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Frame shape: 4-byte big-endian
.B u32
payload length, followed by that many JSON bytes. Length
.B must
be
.BR "<= 1_048_576" .
.IP \(bu 2
Payload type:
.B pcloud_ipc::Request
or
.B pcloud_ipc::RequestEnvelope
(the envelope is a back-compat wrapper that carries an optional
.B traceparent
field; legacy clients sending a bare
.B Request
are still accepted and treated as the trace root).
.IP \(bu 2
Response type:
.B pcloud_ipc::Response
with a typed
.BR ResponseStatus .
.RE
The dispatcher never panics on malformed input; decode errors map to
typed error statuses.
.
.SH DEBUGGING
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard tracing-subscriber envelope. Useful values:
.IP
.B RUST_LOG=pcloud_daemon=debug,pcloud_ipc=debug,pcloud_proto=info
.IP
Module-level trace (\c
.BR =trace )
is very chatty; prefer
.B =debug
for routine operator debugging.
.TP
.B Summary dry-run
Run
.B pcloudd
with no arguments and read the one-shot summary. It names the failing
subsystem if bootstrap fails.
.TP
.B Audit chain verification
.nf
pcloudc audit verify                     # hash chain only
PCLOUD_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY=... pcloudc audit verify   # HMAC + hash
.fi
.TP
.B Common startup failures
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Permission denied" on socket bind
\(em a stale socket remains from a previous run owned by another UID,
or
.I runtime_dir
is not writable by the daemon UID.
.IP \(bu 2
.B "config validation failed: production-plaintext"
\(em
.B PCLOUD_API_MODE=plaintext
was set while
.B PCLOUD_ENV
resolves to
.BR production .
Fix the env, or move to
.BR development .
.IP \(bu 2
.B "vault: file mode 0o644 must be 0o600"
\(em an external actor widened the vault permissions. Rotate the
token and reset the file to
.BR 0600 .
.IP \(bu 2
.B "orphan FUSE mounts detected"
\(em a previous daemon was SIGKILLed. Recover with
.B "pcloudc mount --force-umount <path>"
or set
.B PCLOUD_FORCE_UMOUNT=1
for the next start.
.IP \(bu 2
.B "integrity_check failed"
\(em SQLite store corruption. Stop the daemon, back up
.IR state/ ,
and contact support with the audit log and the
.B pcloudd
summary.
.RE
.
.SH SERVICE MANAGEMENT
.SS systemd (Linux, recommended)
Minimal hardened unit file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[Unit]
Description=pCloud background service
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/usr/bin/pcloudd serve
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5s
TimeoutStopSec=30s
# Optional headless bootstrap:
# LoadCredential=pcloud-rs-token:/etc/pcloud/token
# LoadCredential=pcloud-rs-username:/etc/pcloud/username
# LoadCredential=pcloud-rs-password:/etc/pcloud/password
# Hardening
NoNewPrivileges=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=read-only
PrivateTmp=true
ReadWritePaths=%h/.pcloud %h/.local/state/pcloud %h/.cache/pcloud
UMask=0077

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Operator recipes:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now pcloudd
systemctl status pcloudd
journalctl -u pcloudd -f
sudo systemctl restart pcloudd   # after pcloud.conf changes
.fi
.RE
.PP
For a desktop login install, prefer a
.B --user
unit at
.IR ~/.config/systemd/user/pcloudd.service
driven by
.BR "systemctl --user" .
Use
.B "loginctl enable-linger <user>"
to keep the daemon alive after logout.
.B pcloudd
does not hot-reload; restart after any
.BR pcloud.conf (5)
edit.
.SS launchd (macOS)
User agent at
.IR ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.pcloud.pcloudd.plist
(interactive accounts) or system daemon at
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.pcloud.pcloudd.plist
(headless hosts, owned by root, mode
.BR 0644 ,
.B UserName
= dedicated service account). Load with
.B launchctl load
(or
.B "sudo launchctl load"
for system daemons).
.SS Service Control Manager (Windows)
.B pcloudd.exe
is a console program; wrap it with
.B pcloudd-svc.exe
(the shipped service host) and register via
.BR sc.exe .
Run the service under a dedicated local account, not
.BR LocalSystem .
The wrapper forwards SCM stop as the equivalent of
.B SIGTERM
so graceful drain still applies.
.SS rc.d (FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD)
Drop
.I /usr/local/etc/rc.d/pcloudd
and enable with
.B pcloudd_enable="YES"
in
.IR /etc/rc.conf ;
drive via
.BR "service pcloudd {start|stop|restart|status}" .
.
.SH UPGRADE PATH
.B pcloudd
schema migrations are idempotent and run at bootstrap. Supported path:
.B systemctl stop pcloudd
(graceful drain), replace the binary, review the release notes for
.BR pcloud.conf (5)
changes,
.B pcloudd
(summary dry-run),
.BR "systemctl start pcloudd" .
Downgrade after a schema migration is not supported \(em back up
.I state/store.sqlite3
before upgrading if you might roll back.
.
.SH KNOWN LIMITATIONS (pre-alpha)
This release is pre-alpha and the Rust rewrite is not yet "full
parity" with the legacy C daemon. Concretely:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Mounted-drive runtime (FUSE).
Scaffolded only. Linux mount/unmount, readdir, read-path, write-path,
crash-safe writeback, and integration tests are tracked under
.BR bd\-1du.4 .
The macOS/Windows/BSD mount paths are not yet implemented.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Final parity proof
is still open under
.BR bd\-1du.10 .
Do not rely on release wording that claims "full parity",
"production ready", or "drop-in replacement" until that bead closes.
.IP \(bu 2
.B KMS/HSM.
The
.B Pkcs11Hsm
adapter is a stub. Only the software-backed key wrapper is wired.
.IP \(bu 2
.B OTLP tracing
has been exercised offline against a local sink during bring-up. Live
interop with production OTLP backends (Honeycomb, Datadog, Grafana
Tempo, New Relic) is not certified in this release.
.IP \(bu 2
.B SIGHUP reload
hot-reloads observability flags, rate-limit budgets,
integrity-sweeper schedule, sync poll interval, and
data-residency allow-list. Auth vault, IPC socket, and crypto
master key changes still require a restart.
.IP \(bu 2
.B change_crypto_pass
family,
.BR send_change_user_private ,
and
.B priv_key_flags
remain unimplemented on the crypto runtime.
.RE
See
.I C_FEATURE_PARITY_MATRIX.csv
and
.I STATUS.md
in the repository tree for the authoritative feature ledger.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean exit. For
.B serve
mode: graceful shutdown completed after
.BR SIGTERM / SIGINT .
.TP
.B 1
Any failure: argument parse error, bootstrap failure, signal-handler
install failure, socket bind failure, or fatal error inside the
serve loop. A one-line explanation goes to stderr; the built-in help
text is printed after it. Service managers pick this up in the
journal.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Foreground debug run with verbose logs
.nf
RUST_LOG=pcloud_daemon=debug,pcloud_ipc=debug \\
  PCLOUD_ENV=development \\
  pcloudd serve
.fi
.TP
.B One-shot bootstrap dry-run (no socket bind)
.nf
pcloudd
.fi
Prints the resolved config and each subsystem's health verdict.
.TP
.B Ephemeral test instance
.nf
tmp=$(mktemp -d)
PCLOUD_ROOT=$tmp \\
  PCLOUD_ENV=test \\
  PCLOUD_API_MODE=development \\
  pcloudd serve
.fi
Isolates config/state/runtime/cache under
.IR $tmp .
.TP
.B Headless bootstrap under systemd with LoadCredential
.nf
# /etc/systemd/system/pcloudd.service.d/creds.conf
[Service]
LoadCredential=pcloud-rs-token:/etc/pcloud/token
Environment=PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS=1
.fi
Token file must be
.BR 0600 ,
owner = root (systemd copies it into the per-unit
.BR CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
with restricted modes).
.TP
.B Production unit with metrics scraped via loopback
.nf
[Service]
Environment=PCLOUD_ENV=production
Environment=PCLOUD_METRICS_PORT=9353
ExecStart=/usr/bin/pcloudd serve
.fi
Prometheus job:
.B "static_configs: [{ targets: ['127.0.0.1:9353'] }]" .
.TP
.B Recover from an orphaned FUSE mount at next start
.nf
PCLOUD_FORCE_UMOUNT=1 systemctl start pcloudd
.fi
Or, surgically:
.BR "pcloudc mount --force-umount /path/to/mount" .
.TP
.B Audit verification with an HMAC-chained log
.nf
export PCLOUD_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY=$(cat /etc/pcloud/audit.key)
pcloudc audit verify
.fi
.
